        // owner didn't get it — it went to 0xdead). But we need a token contract.

        // However, we can still test the difference via a different public surface: the function
        // approveTransfer checks lender == loans[loanID_].lender. That doesn't depend on owner().
        // But we can trigger a revert or different behavior via something that branches on owner.

        // The simplest: call delegateVoting which requires msg.sender == owner().
        // In reference, only the actual owner can call it. In bug, only address(0xdead) can call it.
        // So if we prank as the real owner, reference succeeds, bug reverts.
